# No auto-merge; watch every check

Never enable auto-merge. Do not pass `--auto`, call the auto-merge API
(`enablePullRequestAutoMerge`), or turn auto-merge on in the UI.

"Autopilot", "babysit", "watch until green", and "merge when green" mean you
watch the pull request yourself. Wait until every currently attached check has
finished and succeeded, or until a named deadline, whichever comes first.
Required-check lists and branch protection do not define that set. A repository
may allow a merge while important checks are still running.

Bound the wait by the anti-sleep 8h session bound or the CI subscription
`expiresAt`, whichever is shorter. Then stop, report remaining pending or
failed checks, fail closed, and do not merge. Do not wait forever for a
replacement run that may never start.

Subscribe with `cursor-subscriptions-subscribe_github_ci` (or Origin
equivalent) instead of busy-waiting. If you must poll, use a bounded interval
with backoff and a per-call timeout on `gh` / `gh pr checks`. Do not run an
unbounded tight loop.

Failed, pending, cancelled, and timed-out checks cannot be skipped. Ignore a
check only when the platform already reported skipped/neutral (the workflow
did not apply). Name that check and the platform conclusion. A high-confidence
guess that a job "does not apply" is not enough.

Merge only after that wait, and only when the user asked you to merge.
